  "_comment": "The check registry (SPEC INV-306, requirement 307). One entry per file under scripts/ or guardrails/ that a file under skills/ names in command position, plus every module and data file those entries read at run time. A command position is a path preceded on its line by 'python3 ', 'bash ', 'sh ', or a leading './'; every other path mention is prose and keeps its path. guardrails/check-named-checks.py (gate ae) recomputes every field from the tree and reds a disagreement. Field meanings: kind is check, library or data; name is the handle a skill body uses, carried by a check alone; kit is derived from reach, so an empty reach reads ships, a reach naming a path under the pack's machinery directories reads pack-only, and every other reach reads host-optional; root is argument, working-directory or own-tree; reach is what the check reads that nobody handed it, as a pack-relative path or a plain name for a target outside the tree; needs is what the entry reads at run time, as registry keys. Two derivations the design left open and this file settles: a module another entry imports and that carries no 'if __name__' block is a library even when it opens with a shebang line, and a data file the check carries as its own word list or configuration travels in needs alone while a record describing another actor's tree also stands in reach. Seed measurement on 2026-08-06: 32 entries, holding 21 checks, 3 libraries and 8 data files; over the 21 checks, 14 ships, 3 host-optional and 4 pack-only, and 14 record root argument, 2 working-directory and 5 own-tree.",
